.TH MATRIX-RAIN 1 "2026-11-10" "matrix-overlay 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
matrix-rain \- Matrix-style digital rain over every screen on COSMIC/Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B matrix-rain
.RB [ -h ]
.RB [ --version ]
.RB [ --config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ --geometry
.IR SPEC ]
.RI [ MODE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B matrix-rain
dims the desktop and runs The Matrix "digital rain" across every monitor until
you stop it. It is not a screensaver daemon and has no window, tray icon or
background process: it opens one
.IR zwlr_layer_shell_v1
OVERLAY surface per output, grabs the keyboard exclusively, and exits when the
show ends.
.PP
Press
.B Escape
(or click, or run
.B matrix-rain --stop
from a terminal) to bring the desktop back. A second invocation while a show is
running asks the running instance to stop, so the same shortcut toggles.
.PP
Each surface is painted with GLES2 over EGL by a small native client, so the
compositor imports dmabuf buffers instead of copying a CPU buffer every frame.
If that path is unusable on a given compositor, a Cairo through GTK3 fallback is
used instead when its dependencies are installed.
.SH MODES
Exactly one mode may be given. With no mode, the show starts.
.TP
.BR --preflight
Report whether the interpreter, bindings and native client can start a show.
Draws nothing.
.TP
.BR --diagnose
Print one JSON document describing the compositor, the outputs, the rendering
GPU that was selected and why, and any blockers. The probe surface is created and
destroyed without ever attaching a buffer, so nothing is drawn on screen.
.TP
.BR --monitor-list
Print the outputs as
.IR index:name WIDTHxHEIGHT@SCALE .
.TP
.BR --status
Print the live state as JSON (running, pid, outputs, readiness) and whether the
single-instance lock is held.
.TP
.BR --stop
Ask a running show to stop.
.TP
.BR --self-test
Start a bounded show that asserts its own frame budget, then stop. Only sensible
when drawing on the attached screens is acceptable.
.TP
.BR --print-default-config
Write the built-in default configuration to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show the usage summary and exit successfully.
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Print the program version and exit successfully.
.TP
.BR --config " " \fIFILE\fR
Use this configuration file instead of the search order below.
.TP
.BR --geometry " " \fISPEC\fR
Comma separated
.IR name WxH " or " WxH+X+Y
overrides, for tests and for forcing a layout.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The first file that exists wins; nothing is merged.
.TP
.IR $MATRIX_OVERLAY_CONFIG ", " $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/matrix-overlay/config.toml " or " ~/.config/matrix-overlay/config.toml
the user's own file;
.TP
.IR /etc/matrix-overlay/config.toml
the packaged defaults, editable by an administrator.
.PP
The file is re-read while a show is running, so speed, stream density, tail
length, colours, glow, font and glyph set can be tuned live. Unknown keys are
reported and ignored; out-of-range values are clamped and logged.
.SH KEYBINDING
COSMIC has no supported way for a package to register a custom shortcut, so the
trigger is one manual step: COSMIC Settings, Keyboard, View and customize
shortcuts, Custom shortcuts, add a shortcut named
.IR "Matrix rain"
running the command
.B matrix-rain
as a bare word, then press
.BR Ctrl+Shift+M .
The command line is not run by a shell, so it must not contain
.BR $HOME ,
redirections or quoting.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/matrix-overlay.lock
single-instance lock (flock).
.TP
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/matrix-overlay.status.json
live status, for
.BR --status .
.TP
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/matrix-overlay/matrix-rain.log
log, including the reason a show stopped.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
success, including
.BR --help " and " --version .
.TP
.B 1
for
.BR --status " or " --stop
when no show is running. The JSON from
.BR --status " says the same thing; "
the status exists so a script can branch without parsing it.
.TP
.B 2
configuration error, or no Wayland display.
.TP
.B 3
there is no Wayland session to ask, or that session does not offer layer shell.
.TP
.B 4
another instance already holds the lock.
.TP
.B 5
diagnostics could not complete.
.TP
.B 64
bad command line.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
The upstream repository, issue tracker and packaging notes are linked from
.IR /usr/share/metainfo/tech.i2r.matrixoverlay.metainfo.xml .
